.Nm CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_get_time ,
.Nm CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set_time
.Nd Encapsulates the data required to evaluate whether SCTs meet a Certificate Transparency policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Ft CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new_ex
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_free
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft X509*
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_get0_cert
.Fa "const CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set1_cert
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Ft X509*
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_get0_issuer
.Fa "const CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set1_issuer
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "X509 *issuer"
.Fc
.Ft const CTLOG_STORE *
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_get0_log_store
.Fa "const CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set_shared_CTLOG_STORE
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "CTLOG_STORE *log_store"
.Fc
.Ft uint64_t
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_get_time
.Fa "const CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set_time
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "uint64_t time_in_ms"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX
is used by functions that evaluate whether Signed Certificate Timestamps
(SCTs) fulfil a Certificate Transparency (CT) policy.
This policy may be, for example, that at least one valid SCT is
available.
To determine this, an SCT's timestamp and signature must be verified.
This requires:
.Bl -bullet
.It
the public key of the log that issued the SCT
.It
the certificate that the SCT was issued for
.It
the issuer certificate (if the SCT was issued for a pre-certificate)
.It
the current time
.El
.Pp
The above requirements are met using the setters described below.
.Pp
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new_ex
creates an empty policy evaluation context and associates it with the
given library context
.Fa libctx
and property query string
.Fa propq .
.Pp
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new
does the same thing as
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new_ex
except that it uses the default library context and property query
string.
.Pp
The CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX should then be populated using:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set1_cert
to provide the certificate the SCTs were issued for
.Pp
Increments the reference count of the certificate.
.It
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set1_issuer
to provide the issuer certificate
.Pp
Increments the reference count of the certificate.
.It
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set_shared_CTLOG_STORE
to provide a list of logs that are trusted as sources of SCTs
.Pp
Holds a pointer to the CTLOG_STORE, so the CTLOG_STORE must outlive the
CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX.
.It
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_set_time
to set the time SCTs should be compared with to determine if they are
valid
.Pp
The SCT timestamp will be compared to this time to check whether the SCT
was issued in the future.
RFC6962 states that "TLS clients MUST reject SCTs whose timestamp is in
the future".
By default, this will be set to 5 minutes in the future (e.g.
.Xr (time 3
+ 300) * 1000), to allow for clock drift.
.Pp
The time should be in milliseconds since the Unix Epoch.
.El
.Pp
Each setter has a matching getter for accessing the current value.
.Pp
When no longer required, the
.Vt CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX
should be passed to
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_free
to delete it.
If the argument to
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_free
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh NOTES
The issuer certificate only needs to be provided if at least one of the
SCTs was issued for a pre-certificate.
This will be the case for SCTs embedded in a certificate (i.e.
those in an X.509 extension), but may not be the case for SCTs found in
the TLS SCT extension or OCSP response.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new_ex
and
.Fn CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new
will return NULL if malloc fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7
.Sh HISTORY
CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX_new_ex was added in OpenSSL 3.0. All other functions
were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
